This PR introduces caching for models. The way it works is it dynamically caches and creates a hiearchy using the Guild ID. Additionally, contains updating of existing objects.

Also added to the PR is using the cache in some of the event handlers. The other handlers will require a more sophisticated caching logic. 

Lastly, changed some of ID fields in the models. They were set as String when they should all be longs. 

Also removed the `examples` directory as it's redundant. 

example usage:

```java
discord.getCache()
   .getCacheForGuild(guildId)
   .getFromCache(1, Channel.class);
```

Part 2:

Added dynanmic event listeners. Usage:

Create a class in your project for example:

```java
package com.javadiscord.example;

import com.javadiscord.jdi.core.annotations.ChannelCreate;
import com.javadiscord.jdi.core.annotations.EventListener;
import com.javadiscord.jdi.internal.models.channel.Channel;

@EventListener
public class Example {

    @ChannelCreate
    public void example(Channel channel) {
        System.out.printf("Channel created: %s", channel.name());
    }
}
```
This will automatically get picked up and al channel create events will go there.
The binding is handled in `EventCodecHandler`
